  "question": "The resistance of platinum wire at $0°$C is $2\\ \\Omega$ and $6.8\\ \\Omega$ at $80°$C. The temperature coefficient of resistance of the wire is :",
  "diagram": "",
  "diagram_alt": "",
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$3 \\times 10^{-4}\\ °\\text{C}^{-1}$",
      "image": ""
    },
    {
      "text": "$3 \\times 10^{-3}\\ °\\text{C}^{-1}$",
      "image": ""
    },
    {
      "text": "$3 \\times 10^{-2}\\ °\\text{C}^{-1}$",
      "image": ""
    },
    {
      "text": "$3 \\times 10^{-1}\\ °\\text{C}^{-1}$",
      "image": ""
    }
  ],
  "answer": "C",
  "numerical_answer": "",
  "tolerance": "",
  "solution": "$R_t = R_0(1 + \\alpha t)$:\n$$\\alpha = \\frac{R_t - R_0}{R_0\\,t} = \\frac{6.8 - 2}{2 \\times 80} = \\frac{4.8}{160} = 3 \\times 10^{-2}\\ °\\text{C}^{-1}$$",
